{"assets":["/statement-assets/8fe45a58a1274f61f00d49f0791137e5f238b57908bb0b60232dbc6752e5b64e.png","/statement-assets/b545972264a66eb952da139d36477b56530f9783cbea5d07a13e7b994b989970.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1194","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Count The Rectangles"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ segments drawn on a plane; the $$$i$$$-th segment connects two points ($$$x_{i, 1}$$$, $$$y_{i, 1}$$$) and ($$$x_{i, 2}$$$, $$$y_{i, 2}$$$). Each segment is non-degenerate, and is either horizontal or vertical — formally, for every $$$i \\in [1, n]$$$ either $$$x_{i, 1} = x_{i, 2}$$$ or $$$y_{i, 1} = y_{i, 2}$$$ (but only one of these conditions holds). Only segments of different types may intersect: no pair of horizontal segments shares any common points, and no pair of vertical segments shares any common points."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We say that four segments having indices $$$h_1$$$, $$$h_2$$$, $$$v_1$$$ and $$$v_2$$$ such that $$$h_1 \\lt h_2$$$ and $$$v_1 \\lt v_2$$$ form a rectangle if the following conditions hold:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segments $$$h_1$$$ and $$$h_2$$$ are horizontal; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segments $$$v_1$$$ and $$$v_2$$$ are vertical; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segment $$$h_1$$$ intersects with segment $$$v_1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segment $$$h_2$$$ intersects with segment $$$v_1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segment $$$h_1$$$ intersects with segment $$$v_2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" segment $$$h_2$$$ intersects with segment $$$v_2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please calculate the number of ways to choose four segments so they form a rectangle. Note that the conditions $$$h_1 \\lt h_2$$$ and $$$v_1 \\lt v_2$$$ should hold."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 5000$$$) — the number of segments."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then $$$n$$$ lines follow. The $$$i$$$-th line contains four integers $$$x_{i, 1}$$$, $$$y_{i, 1}$$$, $$$x_{i, 2}$$$ and $$$y_{i, 2}$$$ denoting the endpoints of the $$$i$$$-th segment. All coordinates of the endpoints are in the range $$$[-5000, 5000]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that each segment is non-degenerate and is either horizontal or vertical. Furthermore, if two segments share a common point, one of these segments is horizontal, and another one is vertical."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the number of ways to choose four segments so they form a rectangle."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n-1 4 -1 -2\n6 -1 -2 -1\n-2 3 6 3\n2 -2 2 4\n4 -1 4 3\n5 3 5 1\n5 2 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n1 5 1 0\n0 1 5 1\n5 4 0 4\n4 2 4 0\n4 3 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following pictures represent sample cases:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8fe45a58a1274f61f00d49f0791137e5f238b57908bb0b60232dbc6752e5b64e.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b545972264a66eb952da139d36477b56530f9783cbea5d07a13e7b994b989970.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1194E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1194/problem/E"}